<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="2CO" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">2 Corinthians</para>

<para style="toc1">2 Corinthians</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2CO 1"/>

<para style="s">Paul Greets the Corinthians</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Corinthians 1:1–3</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 18:1–11</char></note>Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Jesus Christ</char></note> by the will of God, and Timothy the brother, </para>

<para style="p" vid="2CO 1:1">To the church of God being in Corinth, with all the saints being in all Achaia: <verse eid="2CO 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 1:2"/>Grace to you⁺ and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ. <verse eid="2CO 1:2"/></para>

<para style="s">The God of All Comfort</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 1:3"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of compassions and God of all comfort, <verse eid="2CO 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 1:4"/>the One comforting us in all our tribulation, for us to be able to comfort those in every tribulation through the comfort with which we ourselves are comforted by God, <verse eid="2CO 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 1:5"/>because just as the sufferings of Christ abound to us, so through Christ our comfort also abounds. <verse eid="2CO 1:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 1:6"/>But if we are hard pressed, <char style="add">it is</char> for your⁺ comfort and salvation; if we are comforted, <char style="add">it is</char> for your⁺ comfort, operating in the endurance of the same sufferings that we also suffer. <verse eid="2CO 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 1:7"/>And our hope for you⁺ <char style="add">is</char> sure, knowing that as you⁺ are fellow partakers of the sufferings, so also of the comfort. <verse eid="2CO 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 1:8"/>For we do not want you⁺ to be ignorant brothers, as to our tribulation having happened in Asia,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the province of Asia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. </char></note> that we were weighed down exceedingly, beyond <char style="add">our</char> power, so as for us to despair even to live. <verse eid="2CO 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 1:9"/>But we have had in ourselves the sentence of death, so that we should not be trusting in ourselves, but in God, the One raising the dead, <verse eid="2CO 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 1:10"/>who delivered us from so great a death and will deliver <char style="add">us</char>,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and He continues to deliver (us)</char></note> in whom we have hoped that also He will deliver <char style="add">us</char> still, <verse eid="2CO 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 1:11"/><char style="add">in</char> your⁺ also together helping us by supplication, so that thanks may be given for us<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">given on your behalf</char></note> by many faces for the gracious gift to us through many. <verse eid="2CO 1:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Change of Plans</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 1:12"/>For our boasting is this: The testimony of our conscience, that in the simplicity<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL, TH, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">holiness</char></note> and sincerity of God, and not in fleshly<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">worldly</char></note> wisdom but in the grace of God, we conducted ourselves in the world and more abundantly toward you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 1:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 1:13"/>For we write no other <char style="add">things</char> to you⁺ but what you⁺ read or also understand. And I hope that you⁺ will understand to the end, <verse eid="2CO 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 1:14"/>as also you⁺ understood us in part, so that we are your⁺ boast, even as you⁺ <char style="add">are</char> also ours, in the day of our Lord Jesus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord Jesus</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 1:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 1:15"/>And with this confidence I was purposing to come to you⁺ before, so that you⁺ might have a second grace, <verse eid="2CO 1:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 1:16"/>and through you⁺ to pass through into Macedonia, and to come to you⁺ again from Macedonia, and to be sent forth by you⁺ to Judea. <verse eid="2CO 1:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 1:17"/>Therefore, purposing this, then, did I use lightness? Or do I purpose what I purpose according to flesh, so that with me it may be “Yes, yes” and “No, no”? <verse eid="2CO 1:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 1:18"/>But faithful <char style="add">is</char> God, that our word to you⁺ is not<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">was not</char></note> “Yes” and “No.” <verse eid="2CO 1:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 1:19"/>For the Son of God, Jesus Christ,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Christ Jesus</char></note> having been proclaimed among you⁺ by us—by me and Silvanus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Silas</char></note> and Timothy—was not “Yes” and “No,” but it has been “Yes” in Him. <verse eid="2CO 1:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 1:20"/>For as many as <char style="add">are</char> the promises of God, in Him <char style="add">is</char> the “Yes.” Therefore also through Him<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in Him</char></note> the “Amen” through us <char style="add">is</char> for glory to God. <verse eid="2CO 1:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 1:21"/>Now the One establishing us with you⁺ into Christ, and having anointed us, <char style="add">is</char> God, <verse eid="2CO 1:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="2CO 1:22"/>the One also having sealed us and having given the pledge of the Spirit in our hearts. <verse eid="2CO 1:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="2CO 1:23"/>But I call God as witness upon my soul, that sparing you⁺ I did not yet come to Corinth. <verse eid="2CO 1:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="2CO 1:24"/>Not that we lord it over your⁺ faith, but we are fellow workers with you⁺ of joy; for in the faith you⁺ stand firm. <verse eid="2CO 1:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="2CO 2"/>

<para style="s">Reaffirm Your Love</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 2:1"/>For I decided this within myself, not to come to you⁺ again in grief. <verse eid="2CO 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 2:2"/>For if I grieve you⁺, then who is gladdening me except the one being grieved by me? <verse eid="2CO 2:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 2:3"/>And I wrote<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to you</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> this same thing so that, having come, I might not have grief from <char style="add">those</char> for whom it was necessary for me to rejoice, having been confident in you⁺ all, that my joy is of all of you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 2:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 2:4"/>For out of much tribulation and anguish of heart, I wrote to you⁺ through many tears, not that you⁺ might be grieved, but that you⁺ might know the love that I have more abundantly toward you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 2:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 2:5"/>But if anyone has caused grief, he has not grieved me, but in part (so that I might not be severe) all of you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 2:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 2:6"/>Sufficient to such a one <char style="add">is</char> the punishment that <char style="add">is</char> by the majority, <verse eid="2CO 2:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 2:7"/>so that on the contrary, <char style="add">it is</char> rather for you⁺ to forgive and to comfort <char style="add">him</char>, lest somehow such a one might be overwhelmed by more abundant grief. <verse eid="2CO 2:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 2:8"/>Therefore I exhort you⁺ to confirm love toward him. <verse eid="2CO 2:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 2:9"/>For this indeed also I wrote, so that I might know the proof of you⁺, whether you⁺ are obedient to everything. <verse eid="2CO 2:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 2:10"/>Now to whomever you⁺ forgive anything, I also do; and indeed to whom I have forgiven, if I have forgiven anything, <char style="add">it is</char> on account of you⁺ in the face of Christ, <verse eid="2CO 2:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 2:11"/>so that we should not be exploited by Satan; for we are not ignorant of his schemes. <verse eid="2CO 2:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Triumph in Christ</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 2:12"/>Now having come to Troas for the gospel of Christ, a door also having been opened to me in the Lord, <verse eid="2CO 2:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 2:13"/>I have had no rest in my spirit <char style="add">in</char> my not finding Titus my brother, but having taken leave of them, I went out to Macedonia. <verse eid="2CO 2:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 2:14"/>But thanks <char style="add">be</char> to God, the One always leading us in triumph in Christ and making manifest the fragrance of the knowledge of Him through us in every place. <verse eid="2CO 2:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 2:15"/>For we are a sweet smell of Christ to God among those being saved and among those perishing: <verse eid="2CO 2:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 2:16"/>to one indeed a smell from death to death, but to one a smell from life to life.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">To the one, we are an odor of death and demise; to the other, a fragrance that brings life.</char></note> And who <char style="add">is</char> sufficient for these things? <verse eid="2CO 2:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 2:17"/>For we are not like the many,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">like others</char></note> peddling the word of God, but as from sincerity—but as from God—we speak before God in Christ. <verse eid="2CO 2:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="2CO 3"/>

<para style="s">Ministers of a New Covenant</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 3:1"/>Are we beginning to commend ourselves again? Or like some, do we need letters of recommendation to you⁺ or from you⁺? <verse eid="2CO 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 3:2"/>You⁺ are our letter, having been inscribed in our hearts, being known and being read by all men, <verse eid="2CO 3:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 3:3"/>being revealed that you⁺ are a letter of Christ, having been ministered to by us, having been inscribed not in ink but with the Spirit of the living God, not in tablets of stone but in tablets of fleshly hearts. <verse eid="2CO 3:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 3:4"/>Now we have such confidence through Christ toward God. <verse eid="2CO 3:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 3:5"/>Not that we are sufficient from ourselves to reckon anything as of ourselves, but our sufficiency <char style="add">is</char> of God, <verse eid="2CO 3:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 3:6"/>who also made us sufficient <char style="add">as</char> ministers of a new covenant, not of the letter, but of the Spirit. For the letter kills, but the Spirit gives life. <verse eid="2CO 3:6"/></para>

<para style="s">The Glory of the New CovenantExodus 34:10–35</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 3:7"/>Now if the ministry of death, having been engraved in letters on stones, came into being in glory so as for the sons of Israel not to be able to look intently into the face of Moses on account of the glory of his face that is fading away, <verse eid="2CO 3:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 3:8"/>how will the ministry of the Spirit not be more in glory? <verse eid="2CO 3:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 3:9"/>For if in the ministry of condemnation <char style="add">was</char> glory, much more does the ministry of righteousness abound <char style="add">in</char> glory! <verse eid="2CO 3:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 3:10"/>For even that having been glorious has no glory in this respect, on account of the glory surpassing <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="2CO 3:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 3:11"/>For if that which is fading away <char style="add">was</char> through glory, much more <char style="add">is</char> that remaining in glory! <verse eid="2CO 3:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 3:12"/>Therefore having such a hope, we use much boldness, <verse eid="2CO 3:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 3:13"/>and not as Moses would put a veil over his face for the sons of Israel not to look intently into the end of what <char style="add">was</char> fading away. <verse eid="2CO 3:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 3:14"/>But their minds were hardened; for until the present day, the same veil remains upon the reading of the old covenant, not being unveiled, which is removed in Christ. <verse eid="2CO 3:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 3:15"/>But until today when Moses is read, a veil lies upon their heart. <verse eid="2CO 3:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 3:16"/>But whenever one may turn to the Lord, the veil is taken away. <verse eid="2CO 3:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 3:17"/>Now the Lord is the Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord <char style="add">is</char>, freedom <char style="add">is</char>. <verse eid="2CO 3:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 3:18"/>And we all, having been unveiled in face, reflecting the glory of the Lord, are being transformed into the same image from glory to glory, even as from the Lord, the Spirit. </para>

<para style="p" vid="2CO 3:18"> BYZ and Stephanus TR do not include <char style="add">Or</char> BYZ and TR <char style="add">letters of commendation to you or of commendation from you</char><verse eid="2CO 3:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="2CO 4"/>

<para style="s">The Light of the Gospel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 4:1"/>On account of this, having this ministry, just as we received mercy, we do not grow fainthearted. <verse eid="2CO 4:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 4:2"/>But we renounced the hidden things of shame, not walking in craftiness nor distorting the word of God, but by manifestation of the truth commending ourselves to every conscience of men before God. <verse eid="2CO 4:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 4:3"/>But if indeed our gospel is veiled, it is veiled to those perishing, <verse eid="2CO 4:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 4:4"/>in whom the god of this age blinded the minds of the unbelieving, so as not to shine forth the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP </char><char style="fq" closed="false">so that the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God, might not dawn upon them</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 4:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 4:5"/>For we do not proclaim ourselves, but Christ Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NA </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jesus Christ</char></note> <char style="add">as</char> Lord, and ourselves <char style="add">as</char> your⁺ servants on account of Jesus. <verse eid="2CO 4:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 4:6"/>For God <char style="add">is</char> the One having said, “Light will shine out of darkness,” who shone in our hearts for the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of Jesus Christ.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Genesis 1:3</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL, NE, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the face of Christ</char></note><verse eid="2CO 4:6"/></para>

<para style="s">Treasure in Jars of ClayRomans 6:1–14</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 4:7"/>Now we have this treasure in earthen vessels, so that the supereminence of the power may be from God and not from us, <verse eid="2CO 4:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 4:8"/>being pressed in every <char style="add">way</char> but not being crushed, being perplexed but not despairing, <verse eid="2CO 4:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 4:9"/>being persecuted but not being forsaken, being struck down but not being destroyed, <verse eid="2CO 4:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 4:10"/>always carrying around the death <char style="add">of</char> Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the death of the Lord Jesus</char></note> in the body, so that the life of Jesus also may be revealed in our body. <verse eid="2CO 4:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 4:11"/>For we the living are always being delivered to death on account of Jesus, so that the life of Jesus may also be revealed in our mortal flesh. <verse eid="2CO 4:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 4:12"/>So then, death works in us, but life in you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 4:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 4:13"/>But having the same spirit of faith according to that having been written: “I believed, therefore I spoke,” we also believe, and therefore we speak, <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 116:10 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="2CO 4:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 4:14"/>knowing that the One having raised the Lord Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL </char><char style="fq" closed="false">who raised Jesus</char></note> also will raise us with<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">through</char></note> Jesus and will present <char style="add">us</char> with you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 4:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 4:15"/>For all things <char style="add">are</char> on account of you⁺, so that the grace having increased on account of more <char style="add">people</char> may make abundant the thanksgiving, to the glory of God. <verse eid="2CO 4:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 4:16"/>Therefore we do not grow fainthearted; but if also our outer man decays, yet our inner one<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the inner</char></note> is renewed day and day. <verse eid="2CO 4:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 4:17"/>For the momentary lightness of our affliction is producing for us an eternal weight of glory, from supereminence to supereminence, <verse eid="2CO 4:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 4:18"/>in <char style="add">our</char> not looking at the things being seen, but the things not being seen. For the things being seen <char style="add">are</char> temporary, but the things not being seen <char style="add">are</char> eternal. <verse eid="2CO 4:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 4"/>

<chapter number="5" style="c" sid="2CO 5"/>

<para style="s">Our Eternal Dwelling</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 5:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 8:18–27</char></note>For we know that if our earthly house, the tent, should be torn down, we have a building from God, a house not made with hands, eternal in the heavens. <verse eid="2CO 5:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 5:2"/>For also in this we groan, longing to be clothed with our dwelling that <char style="add">is</char> from heaven, <verse eid="2CO 5:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 5:3"/>if indeed also having been clothed, we will not be found naked. <verse eid="2CO 5:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 5:4"/>For indeed, being in the tent we groan, being burdened, because we do not want to be unclothed but to be clothed, so that the mortal should be swallowed up by life. <verse eid="2CO 5:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 5:5"/>Now the One having prepared us for this very <char style="add">thing</char> <char style="add">is</char> God, the One having given to us the pledge of the Spirit, <verse eid="2CO 5:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 5:6"/>being confident, then, always, and knowing that being at home in the body we are away from the Lord. <verse eid="2CO 5:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 5:7"/>For we walk by faith, not by sight. <verse eid="2CO 5:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 5:8"/>Now we are confident and we are well pleased rather to be away, out of the body, and to be at home with the Lord. <verse eid="2CO 5:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 5:9"/>Therefore also we strive earnestly, whether being at home or being away, to be well-pleasing to Him. <verse eid="2CO 5:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 5:10"/>For it is necessary for us all to appear before the judgment seat of Christ, so that each may receive back the things <char style="add">done</char> through the body according to what he did, whether good or evil. <verse eid="2CO 5:10"/></para>

<para style="s">Ambassadors for Christ</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 5:11"/>Therefore, knowing the fear of the Lord, we persuade men. And we have been made manifest to God, and I hope to have been made manifest in your⁺ consciences also. <verse eid="2CO 5:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 5:12"/>We do not commend<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For we do not commend</char></note> ourselves to you⁺ again, but are giving to you⁺ occasion of boasting on behalf of us, so that you⁺ may have <char style="add">something</char> toward those boasting in appearance and not in heart. <verse eid="2CO 5:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 5:13"/>For if we were beside ourselves, <char style="add">it is</char> to God; and if we are sound-minded, <char style="add">it is</char> for you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 5:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 5:14"/>For the love of Christ compels us, having judged this, that<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">if</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> One died for all, therefore all died. <verse eid="2CO 5:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 5:15"/>And He died for all, that those living no longer should live to themselves, but to the One having died for them<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for all</char></note> and having been raised again. <verse eid="2CO 5:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 5:16"/>Therefore, from now, we know no one according to the flesh. Even if we have known Christ according to the flesh, yet now we know Him <char style="add">thus</char> no longer. <verse eid="2CO 5:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 5:17"/>Therefore if anyone <char style="add">is</char> in Christ, <char style="add">he is</char> a new creation.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a new creature</char></note> The old things passed away; behold, the new things have come into being!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Behold, all things have become new</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 5:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 5:18"/>Now all things <char style="add">are</char> of God, the One having reconciled us to Himself through Christ,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">through Jesus Christ</char></note> and having given to us the ministry of reconciliation: <verse eid="2CO 5:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 5:19"/>how that God was in Christ reconciling the world to Himself, not reckoning to them their trespasses, and having put into us the word of reconciliation. <verse eid="2CO 5:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 5:20"/>Therefore we are ambassadors for Christ, as though God is appealing through us. We implore on behalf of Christ: Be reconciled to God. <verse eid="2CO 5:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 5:21"/>He made<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For He made</char></note> the One not having known sin <char style="add">to be</char> sin<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a sin offering</char></note> for us, so that we might become the righteousness of God in Him. <verse eid="2CO 5:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 5"/>

<chapter number="6" style="c" sid="2CO 6"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s Hardships and God’s Grace</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 6:1"/>And working together,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">As God's fellow workers</char></note> we also exhort you⁺ not to receive the grace of God in vain. <verse eid="2CO 6:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 6:2"/>For He says: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="2CO 6:2">“In the acceptable time I listened to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 6:2">and in the day of salvation I helped you.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="2CO 6:2">Behold, now <char style="add">is</char> the favorable time; behold, now <char style="add">is</char> the day of salvation. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 49:8 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="2CO 6:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 6:3"/>We are giving no cause of stumbling among <char style="add">anyone</char>, so that the ministry should not be blamed, <verse eid="2CO 6:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 6:4"/>but in everything we are commending ourselves as God’s servants: in much endurance, in tribulations, in hardships, in distresses; <verse eid="2CO 6:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 6:5"/>in beatings, in imprisonments, in tumults, in labors, in sleepless nights, in fastings; <verse eid="2CO 6:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 6:6"/>in purity, in knowledge, in patience, in kindness; in the Holy Spirit, in sincere love; <verse eid="2CO 6:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 6:7"/>in the word of truth, in the power of God; through the weapons of righteousness for the right hand and for the left; <verse eid="2CO 6:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 6:8"/>through glory and dishonor, through bad report and good report; as imposters yet true; <verse eid="2CO 6:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 6:9"/>as being unknown yet being well-known; as dying, yet behold, we live; as being disciplined yet not being put to death; <verse eid="2CO 6:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 6:10"/>as being sorrowful yet always rejoicing; as poor yet enriching many; as having nothing and yet possessing everything. <verse eid="2CO 6:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 6:11"/>Our mouth has been open to you⁺, Corinthians; our heart has been enlarged. <verse eid="2CO 6:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 6:12"/>You⁺ are not restrained by us, but you⁺ are restrained in your⁺ <char style="add">own</char> inner parts. <verse eid="2CO 6:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 6:13"/>Now <char style="add">as</char> the same recompense—I speak as to children—you⁺ be enlarged also. <verse eid="2CO 6:13"/></para>

<para style="s">Do Not Be Unequally Yoked</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 6:14"/>Do not become unequally yoked together with unbelievers. For what partnership <char style="add">have</char> righteousness and lawlessness? Or what fellowship <char style="add">has</char> light with darkness? <verse eid="2CO 6:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 6:15"/>And what harmony <char style="add">has</char> Christ with Beliar?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Scrivener’s TR and GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Belial</char></note> Or what part to a believer <char style="add">is</char> with an unbeliever? <verse eid="2CO 6:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 6:16"/>And what agreement <char style="add">has</char> the temple of God with idols? For we are the temple of the living God. As God has said: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="2CO 6:16">“I will dwell in them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 6:16">and I will walk among <char style="add">them</char>, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="2CO 6:16">and I will be their God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 6:16">and they will be My people.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">you</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Leviticus 26:12; Jeremiah 32:38; Ezekiel 37:27</char></note><verse eid="2CO 6:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 6:17"/>“Therefore come out from their midst and be separate, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 6:17">says the Lord, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="2CO 6:17">and touch no unclean <char style="add">thing</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 6:17">and I will receive you⁺.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 52:11; see also Ezekiel 20:34, including LXX.</char></note><verse eid="2CO 6:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 6:18"/>And: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="2CO 6:18">“I will be for a Father to you⁺, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 6:18">and you⁺ will be for sons and daughters to Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 6:18">says the Lord Almighty.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See 2 Samuel 7:14.</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 6:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 6"/>

<chapter number="7" style="c" sid="2CO 7"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s Joy in the Corinthians</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 7:1"/>Therefore having these promises, beloved, we should cleanse ourselves from every defilement of flesh and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of God. <verse eid="2CO 7:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 7:2"/>Make room for us. We wronged no one, we corrupted no one, we took advantage of no one. <verse eid="2CO 7:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 7:3"/>I do not speak for condemnation; for I have before said that you⁺ are in our hearts for <char style="add">us</char> to die together and to live together. <verse eid="2CO 7:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 7:4"/>Much <char style="add">is</char> my boldness toward you⁺; much <char style="add">is</char> my boasting on behalf of you⁺; I have been filled with encouragement; I overabound with joy upon all our tribulation. <verse eid="2CO 7:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 7:5"/>For also of our having come into Macedonia, our flesh had no rest; but we are being pressed in every <char style="add">way</char>: conflicts on the outside, fears within. <verse eid="2CO 7:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 7:6"/>But God, the One comforting the downcast, comforted us in the coming of Titus, <verse eid="2CO 7:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 7:7"/>and not only in his coming, but also in the comfort with which he was comforted over you⁺, declaring to us your⁺ longing, your⁺ mourning, your⁺ zeal for me, so as for me to rejoice the more. <verse eid="2CO 7:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 7:8"/>For if also I grieved you⁺ in the letter, I do not regret <char style="add">it</char>—even if I did regret <char style="add">it</char>; for I see that the letter grieved you⁺, that even if for an hour. <verse eid="2CO 7:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 7:9"/>Now I rejoice, not that you⁺ were grieved, but that you⁺ were grieved unto repentance. For you⁺ were grieved according to God, so that you⁺ might suffer loss in nothing through us. <verse eid="2CO 7:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 7:10"/>For grief according to God works repentance unto salvation without regret; but the grief of the world produces death. <verse eid="2CO 7:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 7:11"/>For behold how much earnestness this same thing—to have been grieved according to God—produced in you⁺: but defense, but indignation, but fear, but longing, but zeal, but avenging! In everything, you⁺ commended yourselves to be innocent in the matter. <verse eid="2CO 7:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 7:12"/>So even if I wrote to you⁺, <char style="add">it was</char> not for the sake of the one having done wrong, nor for the sake of the one having suffered wrong, but for the sake of your⁺ earnestness for us being made manifest to you⁺ before God. <verse eid="2CO 7:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 7:13"/>On account of this, we have been comforted. And upon our comfort, we rejoiced more abundantly rather at the joy of Titus, because his spirit has been refreshed by all of you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 7:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 7:14"/>For if I have boasted anything to him about you⁺, I was not put to shame; but as we spoke all things to you⁺ in truth, so also our boasting to Titus became truth. <verse eid="2CO 7:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 7:15"/>And his affections are more abundantly for you⁺, remembering the obedience of all of you⁺, how you⁺ received him with fear and trembling. <verse eid="2CO 7:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 7:16"/>I rejoice that in everything I am confident in you⁺. </para>

<para style="p" vid="2CO 7:16"> BYZ and TR include <char style="add">you to have been grieved</char>. Scrivener TR <char style="add">our earnestness for you</char> BYZ and TR <char style="add">upon your comfort</char> Scrivener TR <char style="add">I rejoice, therefore,</char><verse eid="2CO 7:16"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 7"/>

<chapter number="8" style="c" sid="2CO 8"/>

<para style="s">Generosity Commended</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 8:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Philippians 4:10–20</char></note>Now we make known to you⁺,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I want you to know about</char></note> brothers, the grace of God having been given in the churches of Macedonia, <verse eid="2CO 8:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 8:2"/>that in much proof of tribulation, the abundance of their joy and of their deep poverty abounded into the riches of their generosity. <verse eid="2CO 8:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 8:3"/>For I testify <char style="add">that</char> according to <char style="add">their</char> power and beyond <char style="add">their</char> power, of their own accord, <verse eid="2CO 8:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 8:4"/>with much entreaty <char style="add">they were</char> imploring us for the grace and the fellowship of the service to the saints. <verse eid="2CO 8:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 8:5"/>And not even as we expected, but they gave themselves first to the Lord and to us by the will of God. <verse eid="2CO 8:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 8:6"/>Accordingly, we exhorted Titus that just as he began before, so also he might complete to you⁺ also this grace, <verse eid="2CO 8:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 8:7"/>but just as you⁺ abound in everything—in faith and word and knowledge and all earnestness and in the love from us in you⁺<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in your love for us</char></note>—that also you⁺ may abound in this grace. <verse eid="2CO 8:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 8:8"/>I do not speak as a command, but proving the genuineness of your⁺ love through the earnestness of others also. <verse eid="2CO 8:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 8:9"/>For you⁺ know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that being rich, on account of you⁺<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on account of us</char></note> He became poor, so that you⁺ by that poverty might be enriched. <verse eid="2CO 8:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 8:10"/>And I give a judgment in this <char style="add">matter</char>, for this is profitable for you⁺, who not only began before to do, but also to will, from a year ago. <verse eid="2CO 8:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 8:11"/>And now also complete the doing, so that just as <char style="add">there was</char> the readiness to will, so also <char style="add">there may be</char> to complete out of that which you have. <verse eid="2CO 8:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 8:12"/>For if the readiness is present, <char style="add">it is</char> acceptable as if he may have, not as he does not have. <verse eid="2CO 8:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 8:13"/>For <char style="add">it is</char> not that to others <char style="add">is</char> relief <char style="add">and</char> for you⁺ tribulation, but of equality. <verse eid="2CO 8:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 8:14"/>At the present time, your⁺ abundance <char style="add">is</char> for their need, so that their abundance also may be for your⁺ need, so that there may be equality. <verse eid="2CO 8:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 8:15"/>As it has been written: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="2CO 8:15">“The one who <char style="add">gathered</char> much did not abound, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 8:15">and the one who <char style="add">gathered</char> little did not lack.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 16:18</char></note><verse eid="2CO 8:15"/></para>

<para style="s">Titus CommendedTitus 1:1–4</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 8:16"/>But thanks to God, the One putting the same earnestness for you⁺ in the heart of Titus. <verse eid="2CO 8:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 8:17"/>For indeed he accepted the exhortation, but being more earnest, of his own accord he went out to you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 8:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 8:18"/>And we sent with him the brother whose praise in the gospel <char style="add">is</char> through all of the churches, <verse eid="2CO 8:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 8:19"/>and not only <char style="add">that</char>, but also having been appointed by the churches, <char style="add">he is</char> our fellow traveler with this grace that <char style="add">is</char> being ministered by us<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See 1 Corinthians 16:3–4.</char></note> toward the glory of the Lord Himself and <char style="add">to</char> our readiness, <verse eid="2CO 8:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 8:20"/>avoiding this, lest anyone should blame us in this abundance being ministered by us. <verse eid="2CO 8:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 8:21"/>For we are giving forethought to what is right, not only before the Lord but also before men. <verse eid="2CO 8:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="2CO 8:22"/>Now we sent with them our brother, whom we proved often in many things to be earnest, but now much more earnest by <char style="add">his</char> confidence that <char style="add">is</char> in you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 8:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="2CO 8:23"/>Whether as regards Titus my partner and fellow worker for you⁺. or our brothers, <char style="add">they are</char> apostles<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">messengers</char></note> of the churches, the glory of Christ— <verse eid="2CO 8:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="2CO 8:24"/>the demonstration therefore of your⁺ love and of our boasting on behalf of you⁺ to them, demonstrated to the face of the churches. <verse eid="2CO 8:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 8"/>

<chapter number="9" style="c" sid="2CO 9"/>

<para style="s">God Loves a Cheerful Giver</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 9:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Corinthians 16:1–4</char></note>For indeed, concerning the ministry to the saints, it is superfluous for me to write to you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 9:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 9:2"/>For I know your⁺ readiness, which I boast of to Macedonians on behalf of you⁺, that Achaia has been prepared from a year ago, and your⁺ zeal provoked the greater part. <verse eid="2CO 9:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 9:3"/>But I sent the brothers so that our boasting that <char style="add">is</char> on behalf of you⁺ in this matter should not be made void, so that you⁺ may be prepared, as I have been saying— <verse eid="2CO 9:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 9:4"/>lest perhaps if Macedonians should come with me and should find you⁺ unprepared, we would be put to shame—not that we might say you⁺—in this confidence.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in our boasting</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 9:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 9:5"/>Therefore I deemed <char style="add">it</char> necessary to exhort the brothers that they should go before to you⁺ and should complete beforehand your⁺ foreannounced blessing, thus <char style="add">for</char> this to be ready as a blessing and not as covetousness. <verse eid="2CO 9:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 9:6"/>Now this: The one sowing sparingly will also reap sparingly, and the one sowing upon blessings will also reap upon blessings, <verse eid="2CO 9:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 9:7"/>each as he has purposed in the heart, not out of grief or out of necessity. For God loves a cheerful giver.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as he purposes</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Proverbs 22:8, LXX addition.</char></note><verse eid="2CO 9:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 9:8"/>And God <char style="add">is</char> able to make all grace abound to you⁺, so that in every <char style="add">way</char>, always, having all sufficiency, you⁺ may abound to every good work. <verse eid="2CO 9:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 9:9"/>As it has been written: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="2CO 9:9">“He scattered abroad; He gave to the poor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="2CO 9:9">His righteousness remains to the age.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 112:9</char></note><verse eid="2CO 9:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 9:10"/>Now the One supplying seed to the one sowing and bread for food will supply and will multiply your⁺ seed and will increase the fruits of your⁺ righteousness, <verse eid="2CO 9:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 9:11"/>being enriched in every <char style="add">way</char> to all generosity, which produces through us thanksgiving to God. <verse eid="2CO 9:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 9:12"/>For the ministry of this service is not only supplying the needs of the saints, but is also abounding through many thanksgivings to God, <verse eid="2CO 9:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 9:13"/>through the proof of this ministry, glorifying God upon your⁺ submission of confession to the gospel of Christ, and the generosity of the fellowship to them and to all. <verse eid="2CO 9:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 9:14"/>And their supplication <char style="add">is</char> for you⁺, longing for you⁺ on account of the surpassing grace of God upon you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 9:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 9:15"/>Thanks <char style="add">be</char> to God for His indescribable gift! <verse eid="2CO 9:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 9"/>

<chapter number="10" style="c" sid="2CO 10"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s Apostolic Authority</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 10:1"/>Now I, Paul, myself exhort you⁺ by the mildness and gentleness of Christ—<char style="add">I</char> who indeed as to presence <char style="add">am</char> humble among you⁺, but being absent am bold toward you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 10:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 10:2"/>Now I implore <char style="add">you</char> that being present, <char style="add">I need</char> not to be bold with the confidence with which I reckon to be daring toward some reckoning us as walking according to the flesh. <verse eid="2CO 10:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 10:3"/>For walking in flesh, we do not wage war according to the flesh. <verse eid="2CO 10:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 10:4"/>For the weapons of our warfare <char style="add">are</char> not fleshly, but powerful before God toward the tearing down of strongholds, <verse eid="2CO 10:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 10:5"/>tearing down arguments and every high thing lifting itself up against the knowledge of God, and taking captive every thought into the obedience of Christ, <verse eid="2CO 10:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 10:6"/>and having readiness within to avenge all disobedience, when your⁺ obedience shall have been fulfilled. <verse eid="2CO 10:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 10:7"/>You⁺ are looking at things according to appearance. If anyone has been persuaded in himself to be of Christ, let him reckon this upon himself again, that as he <char style="add">is</char> of Christ, so also <char style="add">are</char> we. <verse eid="2CO 10:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 10:8"/>For even if I should boast somewhat more abundantly concerning our authority, which the Lord gave <char style="add">us</char> for building up and not for tearing you⁺ down, I will not be ashamed, <verse eid="2CO 10:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 10:9"/>so that I might not seem as if to frighten you⁺ through the letters. <verse eid="2CO 10:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 10:10"/>For they say, “The letters indeed <char style="add">are</char> weighty and strong, but the presence of the body <char style="add">is</char> weak, and the word is of no account.” <verse eid="2CO 10:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 10:11"/>Let such a one reckon this, that such as we are in word through letters being absent, also such <char style="add">we are</char> in deed being present. <verse eid="2CO 10:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 10:12"/>For we do not dare to classify or to compare ourselves <char style="add">with</char> some commending themselves. But these, measuring themselves by themselves and comparing themselves with themselves, do not understand. <verse eid="2CO 10:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 10:13"/>But we will not boast unto the things without measure, but according to the measure of the area that God apportioned to us, a measure to reach even as far as you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 10:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 10:14"/>For we are not overextending ourselves, as not reaching to you⁺. For we came also as far as you⁺ in the gospel of Christ, <verse eid="2CO 10:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 10:15"/>not boasting unto the things without measure in others’ labors, but having hope <char style="add">of</char> your⁺ faith increasing among you⁺ to be enlarged according to our area, to abundance, <verse eid="2CO 10:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 10:16"/>so as to preach the gospel <char style="add">in</char> the <char style="add">places</char> beyond you⁺, not to boast in the things ready in another’s area. <verse eid="2CO 10:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 10:17"/>But, “The one boasting, let him boast in the Lord.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Jeremiah 9:24</char></note><verse eid="2CO 10:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 10:18"/>For the one commending himself, that one is not approved, but the one whom the Lord commends. <verse eid="2CO 10:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 10"/>

<chapter number="11" style="c" sid="2CO 11"/>

<para style="s">Paul and the False Apostles</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 11:1"/>I wish you⁺ were bearing with me in a little foolishness, but you⁺ also bear with me. <verse eid="2CO 11:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 11:2"/>For I am jealous <char style="add">as to</char> you⁺ with the jealousy of God. For I betrothed you⁺ to one husband, to present a pure virgin to Christ. <verse eid="2CO 11:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 11:3"/>But I fear, lest somehow, as the serpent deceived Eve in his craftiness, your⁺ minds might be corrupted from the simplicity and the purity<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and the purity</char></note> that <char style="add">is</char> to Christ. <verse eid="2CO 11:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 11:4"/>For if indeed the one coming proclaims another Jesus whom we did not proclaim, or you⁺ receive a different spirit that you⁺ did not receive, or a different gospel that you⁺ did not accept, you⁺ bear with <char style="add">it</char> well. <verse eid="2CO 11:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 11:5"/>For I reckon in nothing to have been lacking <char style="add">to</char> the “most eminent apostles.” <verse eid="2CO 11:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 11:6"/>But even if <char style="add">I am</char> unskilled in word, yet not in knowledge; but in every <char style="add">way</char>, we were made manifest to you⁺ in all things. <verse eid="2CO 11:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 11:7"/>Or did I commit a sin, humbling myself so that you⁺ might be exalted, because I preached the gospel of God to you⁺ freely? <verse eid="2CO 11:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 11:8"/>I robbed other churches, having received support for ministry to you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 11:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 11:9"/>And being present with you⁺ and having been in need, I burdened no one; for the brothers having come from Macedonia supplied my need, and in everything I kept and will keep myself unburdensome to you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 11:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 11:10"/>The truth of Christ is in me, that this boasting of mine will not be stopped in the regions of Achaia. <verse eid="2CO 11:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 11:11"/>Because of what? Because I do not love you⁺? God knows <char style="add">I do</char>! <verse eid="2CO 11:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 11:12"/>But what I do, I also will do, so that I might cut off the opportunity of those wanting an opportunity that in what they boast they might be found according as also we. <verse eid="2CO 11:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 11:13"/>For such <char style="add">are</char> false apostles, deceitful workers, disguising themselves as apostles of Christ. <verse eid="2CO 11:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 11:14"/>And no wonder, for Satan himself disguises himself as an angel of light. <verse eid="2CO 11:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 11:15"/>Therefore <char style="add">it is</char> not great if his servants also disguise themselves as servants of righteousness, whose end will be according to their works. <verse eid="2CO 11:15"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Suffering and ServiceColossians 1:24–29</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 11:16"/>Again I say, no one should think me to be a fool; but if otherwise, receive me even as a fool, that I also may boast a little. <verse eid="2CO 11:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 11:17"/>What I am speaking, I am not speaking according to the Lord, but as in foolishness, in this confidence of boasting. <verse eid="2CO 11:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 11:18"/>Since many boast according to the flesh, I also will boast. <verse eid="2CO 11:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 11:19"/>For gladly you⁺ bear with fools—being wise! <verse eid="2CO 11:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 11:20"/>For you⁺ bear with <char style="add">it</char> if anyone enslaves you⁺, if anyone devours <char style="add">you</char>, if anyone takes <char style="add">from you</char>, if anyone lifts himself up, if anyone strikes you⁺ in the face. <verse eid="2CO 11:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 11:21"/>I speak as to dishonor, as that we have been weak! But in that which anyone may dare—I speak in foolishness—I also dare. <verse eid="2CO 11:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="2CO 11:22"/>Are they Hebrews? I also. Are they Israelites? I also. Are they seed of Abraham? I also. <verse eid="2CO 11:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="2CO 11:23"/>Are they servants of Christ? I speak as being beside myself—I <char style="add">too</char> above measure: in labors more abundantly, in imprisonments more abundantly, in beatings surpassingly,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in worse beatings, in more imprisonments</char></note> in deaths often. <verse eid="2CO 11:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="2CO 11:24"/>Five times I received from the Jews forty <char style="add">lashes</char> minus one. <verse eid="2CO 11:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="2CO 11:25"/>Three times I was beaten with rods, once I was stoned, three times I was shipwrecked. I have passed a night and a day in the deep; <verse eid="2CO 11:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="2CO 11:26"/>in journeyings often, in dangers of rivers, in dangers of robbers; in dangers from kindred, in dangers from the Gentiles; in dangers in the city, in dangers in the wilderness;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">desert</char></note> in dangers in the sea, in dangers among false brothers; <verse eid="2CO 11:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="2CO 11:27"/>in labor and toil, in sleepless <char style="add">nights</char> often; in hunger and thirst, in fastings often; in cold and nakedness. <verse eid="2CO 11:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="2CO 11:28"/>Apart from the external things, the crowding on me on every day <char style="add">is</char> the care of all the churches. <verse eid="2CO 11:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="2CO 11:29"/>Who is weak, and I am not weak? Who is caused to stumble, and I am not burned? <verse eid="2CO 11:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="2CO 11:30"/>If it is necessary to boast, I will boast <char style="add">in</char> the things of my weakness. <verse eid="2CO 11:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="2CO 11:31"/>The God and Father of the Lord Jesus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord Jesus Christ</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; TR and GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of our Lord Jesus Christ</char></note> the One being blessed to the ages,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">worthy of praise forever</char></note> knows that I am not lying. <verse eid="2CO 11:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="2CO 11:32"/>In Damascus the governor under King Aretas was guarding the city of the Damascenes to seize me.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">wishing to seize me</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 11:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="2CO 11:33"/>But I was let down in a basket through a window through the wall, and I escaped his hands. <verse eid="2CO 11:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 11"/>

<chapter number="12" style="c" sid="2CO 12"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s Revelation</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 12:1"/>It is necessary to boast; it is not profitable indeed,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Surely it is not beneficial for me to boast,</char></note> but I will go to visions and revelations of the Lord. <verse eid="2CO 12:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 12:2"/>I know a man in Christ, fourteen years ago—whether in the body, I do not know, or out of the body, I do not know; God knows—such a man, having been caught up to the third heaven. <verse eid="2CO 12:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 12:3"/>And I know such a man—whether in the body or apart from<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">out of</char></note> the body, I do not know; God knows— <verse eid="2CO 12:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 12:4"/>that he was caught up into Paradise,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Luke 23:43 and Revelation 2:7</char></note> and he heard inexpressible words, not being permitted to man to speak. <verse eid="2CO 12:4"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Thorn and God’s Grace</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 12:5"/>On behalf of such a man I will boast; but on behalf of myself I will not boast, except in the weaknesses. <verse eid="2CO 12:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 12:6"/>For if I should want to boast, I will not be a fool, for I will be speaking the truth. But I refrain, lest anyone should reckon to me above what he sees in me or anything he hears of me, <verse eid="2CO 12:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 12:7"/>and the surpassingness of the revelations. Therefore, so that I should not be over-exalted,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some translators end the previous paragraph after verse 6, and begin verse 7 with </char><char style="fq" closed="false">So to keep me from becoming conceited because of these surpassingly great revelations,</char></note> a thorn in <char style="add">my</char> flesh was given to me, a messenger of Satan, that he might buffet me, so that I should not be over-exalted. <verse eid="2CO 12:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 12:8"/>Three times I entreated the Lord for this, that it might depart from me. <verse eid="2CO 12:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 12:9"/>And He has said to me, <char style="wj">“My grace suffices for you, for the power is perfected in weakness.”</char> Most gladly, therefore, rather, I will boast in my weaknesses, so that the power of Christ may rest upon me. <verse eid="2CO 12:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 12:10"/>Therefore I am well pleased in weaknesses, in insults, in hardships, in persecutions and difficulties—for Christ; for when I may be weak, then I am powerful. <verse eid="2CO 12:10"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Concern for the Corinthians</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 12:11"/>I have become a fool;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in my boasting</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> you⁺ compelled me. For I ought to have been commended by you⁺. For in nothing was I lacking <char style="add">to</char> the “most eminent apostles,” even if I am nothing. <verse eid="2CO 12:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 12:12"/>Indeed, the signs of the apostle were performed among you⁺ in all perseverance, both in signs and wonders and miracles. <verse eid="2CO 12:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 12:13"/>For <char style="add">in</char> what is it that you⁺ were inferior beyond the rest <char style="add">of</char> the churches, except that I myself did not burden you⁺? Forgive me this wrong! <verse eid="2CO 12:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 12:14"/>Behold, this third time I am ready to come to you⁺, and I will not be a burden.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to you</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> For I do not seek what <char style="add">is</char> yours⁺, but you⁺. For the children ought not to treasure up for the parents, but the parents for the children. <verse eid="2CO 12:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2CO 12:15"/>Now I will spend most gladly, and will be utterly spent for your⁺ souls.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">souls, even if the more I love you, the less I am loved.</char></note> If loving you⁺ more abundantly, am I loved less? <verse eid="2CO 12:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2CO 12:16"/>But be it so, I did not burden you⁺; but being crafty, I took you⁺ by trickery. <verse eid="2CO 12:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2CO 12:17"/>By any of whom I have sent to you⁺, did I take advantage of you⁺ by him? <verse eid="2CO 12:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2CO 12:18"/>I exhorted Titus <char style="add">to go</char>, and I sent with <char style="add">him</char> the brother. Did Titus take advantage of you⁺? Did we not walk in the same Spirit? Not in the same footsteps?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Did we not walk in the same Spirit and follow in the same footsteps?</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 12:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="2CO 12:19"/>Do you⁺ think all along<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Do you still think</char></note> that we are making a defense to you⁺? We speak in Christ before God, and all things, beloved, for your⁺ edification. <verse eid="2CO 12:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="2CO 12:20"/>For I fear lest somehow, having come, I might not find you⁺ such as I wish, and I might be found by you⁺ such as you⁺ do not wish; lest somehow <char style="add">there is</char> strife,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NA, F35, SBL, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">quarreling</char></note> jealousy,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">jealousies</char></note> rage, rivalries, slander, gossip, conceit, disorder; <verse eid="2CO 12:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="2CO 12:21"/>lest <char style="add">on</char> my having come again, my God should humble me as to you⁺, and I should mourn many of those having before sinned and not having repented of the impurity and sexual immorality and sensuality that they have practiced. <verse eid="2CO 12:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 12"/>

<chapter number="13" style="c" sid="2CO 13"/>

<para style="s">Examine Yourselves</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2CO 13:1"/>This third <char style="add">time</char> I am coming to you⁺. “On the mouth of two or three witnesses every word will be established.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Deuteronomy 19:15</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 13:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2CO 13:2"/>I have said before, and I say <char style="add">it</char> before as being present the second time and being absent now,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I write </char></note> to those having sinned before and to all the rest, that if I come to the <char style="add">same</char> again, I will not spare <char style="add">anyone</char>, <verse eid="2CO 13:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2CO 13:3"/>since you⁺ seek proof of Christ speaking in me, who is not weak toward you⁺ but is powerful among you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 13:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2CO 13:4"/>For<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">although</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> also He was crucified out of weakness, yet He lives out of God's power. For we also are weak in Him, but we will live with Him out of God’s power toward you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 13:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2CO 13:5"/>Test yourselves, whether you⁺ are in the faith; examine yourselves. Or do you⁺ not recognize yourselves that Jesus Christ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Christ Jesus</char></note> <char style="add">is</char> in you⁺?—unless you⁺ are unapproved. <verse eid="2CO 13:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2CO 13:6"/>And I trust that you⁺ will learn that we are not unapproved. <verse eid="2CO 13:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2CO 13:7"/>Now we pray<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I pray</char></note> to God <char style="add">for</char> you⁺ to do nothing wrong, not that we might appear approved, but that you⁺ may do what <char style="add">is</char> right, though we might appear as unapproved. <verse eid="2CO 13:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2CO 13:8"/>For we have no power against the truth, but for the truth. <verse eid="2CO 13:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2CO 13:9"/>For we rejoice when we may be weak but you⁺ may be powerful. This also we pray for: your⁺ perfection. <verse eid="2CO 13:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2CO 13:10"/>Because of this, I write these things being absent, so that being present I should not treat <char style="add">you</char> severely according to the authority that the Lord gave me for building up and not for tearing down. <verse eid="2CO 13:10"/></para>

<para style="s">Benediction and Farewell</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2CO 13:11"/>Finally, brothers, rejoice! Be perfected, be exhorted,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">encourage one another</char></note> <char style="add">be of</char> the same mind, be at peace. And the God of love and peace will be with you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 13:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2CO 13:12"/>Greet one another with a holy kiss. <verse eid="2CO 13:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2CO 13:13"/>All the saints greet you⁺. <verse eid="2CO 13:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2CO 13:14"/>The grace of the<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our</char></note> Lord Jesus Christ, and the love of God, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit <char style="add">be</char> with all of you⁺.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Texts vary in verse numbering for the last three verses of this chapter. BYZ and TR end with </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Amen</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="2CO 13:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="2CO 13"/>

</usx>
